From a9c032a2dda5f241f7801fa4e4ef899a51492007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:43:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diar: run_head_isolated - sound oracle for the head
 (final_norm..sigmoid)

Same idea as run_layer0_isolated/run_encoder_isolated, for the "head" that turns the encoder's output into
per-frame speaker probabilities (final_norm -> encoder_projection -> subpixel_upsample conv1d -> relu ->
head_hidden -> relu -> speaker_head -> sigmoid). Takes the encoder's real output directly rather than
recomputing it. probabilities is the whole graph's terminal node (nothing computed after it), so unlike the
per-layer stages it was already sound by construction - this just gives a standalone rebuild to diff a
CrispASR port against, and confirms the module-call sequence read from encoder.cpp is exactly right.

Verified: byte-identical (max abs diff 0.0) to production's real probabilities on bilingual_multispk_57s.wav
across all three windows in the clip. AUDIOCPP_HEAD_ISOLATED triggers it; also dumps probabilities.f32
(production's own) unconditionally alongside the existing AUDIOCPP_DUMP_LAYER0 files. Production path
unaffected when unset (confirmed via the existing turns.json byte-identity check).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
